.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pepe-logs 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-logs \- Read nginx logs: requests per second now, against each minute, hour and day
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe logs\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-exact\-paths\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read nginx logs: requests per second now, against each minute, hour and day
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
The access log\*(Aqs log_format as nginx.conf has it, on one line, when it isn\*(Aqt `combined`: \*(Aq$remote_addr [$time_local] "$request" $status $request_time\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<TIME>\fR [default: 60s]
What "now" is measured over, e.g. 10s, 1m, 5m
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
How far back to start, e.g. 90m, 24h, 7d. At a terminal a log that is being written is shown live, from five minutes back, without it
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Read all of the log before following it, however far back it goes
.TP
\fB\-\-exact\-paths\fR
Count /items/1 and /items/2 apart. Without it the numbers and ids in a path count as one, /items/*
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 10]
Rows in each table of the report
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Count only the requests to these paths, with * for any run of characters: /api/*, /login; repeat for more. An error log line counts when its request does
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fI<CODES>\fR
Count only the requests that answered these: 404, 5xx, 4xx,503; repeat for more. Error log lines are still counted
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI<HOST>\fR
Count only the requests to these hosts (the log\*(Aqs $host): shop.test exactly, .example.com for it and every host under it; repeat for more
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
Leave out what is newer than this, e.g. 1h for up to an hour ago; with \-\-since, a stretch in the past. A log read up to a time in the past isn\*(Aqt followed
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILES\fR]
Access and error logs, rotated ones too; `\-` or nothing reads what is piped in, and with nothing at all nginx\*(Aqs own in /var/log/nginx
